{title: To God Be the Glory}
{artist: Fanny J. Crosby (1820-1915)}
{key: G}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{sov: Verse 1}
To [G]God be the glory, great [D]things He hath [G]done;
So [C]loved He the [G]world that He [A]gave us His [D]Son,
Who [G]yielded His life an a[C]tonement for sin,
And [G]opened the life gate that [D]all may go [G]in.
{eov}

{soc}
[G]Praise the Lord, praise the Lord, let the [D]earth hear His voice!
[D]Praise the Lord, praise the Lord, let the [G]people re[G7]joice!
O [C]come to the Father through [G]Jesus the [Em]Son,
And [G]give Him the glory, great [D]things He hath [G]done.
{eoc}

{sov: Verse 2}
O [G]perfect redemption, the [D]purchase of [G]blood,
To [C]every be[G]liever the [A]promise of [D]God;
The [G]vilest offender who [C]truly be[Am]lieves,
That [G]moment from Jesus a [D]pardon re[G]ceives.
{eov}

{soc}
[G]Praise the Lord, praise the Lord, let the [D]earth hear His voice!
[D]Praise the Lord, praise the Lord, let the [G]people re[G7]joice!
O [C]come to the Father through [G]Jesus the [Em]Son,
And [G]give Him the glory, great [D]things He hath [G]done.
{eoc}

{sov: Verse 3}
Great [G]things He hath taught us, great [D]things He hath [G]done,
And [C]great our re[G]joicing through [A]Jesus the [D]Son;
But [G]purer, and higher, and [C]greater will be
Our [G]wonder, our victory, when [D]Jesus we [G]see.
{eov}

{soc}
[G]Praise the Lord, praise the Lord, let the [D]earth hear His voice!
[D]Praise the Lord, praise the Lord, let the [G]people re[G7]joice!
O [C]come to the Father through [G]Jesus the [Em]Son,
And [G]give Him the glory, great [D]things He hath [G]done.
